  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Starch is formed from alpha glucose, while cellulose is made of beta glucose. The differences in the linkages lead to variances in 3-D structure and function. Starch can be straight or branched and is used as energy storage for plants because it can form compact structures and is easily broken down.</p><p>Nucleic acids are made of nitrogen-containing bases, phosphate groups, and sugar molecules. Each type of nucleic acid has a distinctive structure and plays a different role in our cells. A nucleotide is the basic building block of nucleic acids (RNA and DNA).</p><p>Proteins are made up of hundreds or thousands of smaller units called amino acids, which are attached to one another in long chains. There are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math> different types of amino acids that can be combined to make a protein.</p><p>Hence, the answer is option D.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
